---
description: Calendars disable past dates unless past dates are explicitly allowed.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Calendar dates

Do not let people pick a date before today unless the product needs it. `Calendar` and `DatePicker` already disable past days by default. Keep that default. Pass `allowPast` only when a past date is a real requirement.

```tsx
// BAD
<Calendar mode="single" allowPast />
<DatePicker allowPast value={dueDate} onChange={setDueDate} />

// GOOD
<Calendar mode="single" />
<DatePicker value={dueDate} onChange={setDueDate} />

// GOOD, past dates are required
<Calendar mode="single" allowPast />
```
